Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 06:12:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): borrow draft placement only at captured tile
 boundary [daveey]

Focus alone does not imply that a tile borrowed the main draft workspace.
Right splits and cwd-less center tiles never capture that boundary, so resolve
main's draft placement from the live pre-existing cwd inputs in those cases.
Retain snapshot isolation only for a captured, still-open tile at its borrowed cwd.

Add the two reviewer sequences through real tile actions, mounted rows and real
first-send action. Both fail on 007aa2ce (Home instead of project p1) while send
cwd remains /repo; both pass with this display-only repair. Rename and document
the intentionally divergent captured-center-tile display/send policy.

Proof: focused 37 tests; sidebar 81 files/1095 tests; full tsc --noEmit;
scripts/check --base origin/main all 21 checks. Send cwd and optimistic upsert
blocks remain unchanged vs main. Independent new-head review and CI required.
